//www.dhs.gov/publications-library/preventing-terrorism-and-targeted-violence)\n        *   [Privacy](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/privacy)\n        *   [REAL ID](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/real-id)\n        *   [Resilience](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/resilience)\n        *   [Science and Technology](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/science-and-technology)\n        *   [Trade and Economic Security](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/trade-and-economic-security)\n        *   [Transportation Security](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/transportation-security)\n        *   [Weapons of Mass Destruction](https://www.dhs.gov/publications-library/weapons-of-mass-destruction)\n\n    *   [Social Media](https://www.dhs.gov/social-media-directory \"Social Media\")\n    *   [Subscribe](https://public.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHS/subscriber/new)\n\n# During Easter Weekend, ICE Arrests Murderers, Multiple Pedophiles, and Drug Traffickers\n\n**Release Date:**April 6, 2026\n\nWASHINGTON –– While many Americans across the country were celebrating Easter over the weekend, the brave men and women of U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) were arresting some of the worst of the worst criminal illegal aliens including murderers, pedophiles, and drug traffickers.\n\n_“Even on the Holy day of Easter, ICE does not take a day off. While Americans celebrated Easter with their families, ICE officers were risking their lives to arrest the worst of the worst,”_ said **Acting Assistant Secretary Lauren Bis**. _“Some of the Easter weekend arrests included murderers, pedophiles, and drug traffickers. Under the leadership of President Trump and Secretary Mullin, DHS is committed to protecting our homeland and will not stop getting criminals out of communities.”_\n\nArrests over the weekend include:\n\nImage\n\n![Image 5: Wilson Zuniga-Ayala, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW1_2.png.webp?itok=mybozsI8)\n\nWilson Zuniga-Ayala, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador, with **11 convictions for crimes including burglary and larceny.**\n\nImage\n\n![Image 6: Rodolfo Lorenzo-Castro, a criminal illegal alien from Guatemala](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW2_2.png.webp?itok=fZPnuGCT)\n\nRodolfo Lorenzo-Castro, a criminal illegal alien from Guatemala, convicted for **manslaughter with a weapon** in Tampa, Florida.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 7: Reinier Fuentes-Armentero, a criminal illegal alien from Cuba](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW3_2.png.webp?itok=iYFW71po)\n\nReinier Fuentes-Armentero, a criminal illegal alien from Cuba, convicted for **FOUR counts** of **possessing, controlling or intentionally viewing sexual performance by a child** in Palm Beach, Florida.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 8: Victor Asuncion, a criminal illegal alien from the Philippines](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW4_1.png.webp?itok=qknWBluB)\n\nVictor Asuncion, a criminal illegal alien from the Philippines, convicted for **forcible lewd act upon a child** in the California Superior Court of Contra Costa, Martinez, California.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 9: Arturo Barrios-Medina, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW5_2.png.webp?itok=zxZlREjW)\n\nArturo Barrios-Medina, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted for **possession of child pornography and selling/renting/loaning/giving obscene material** to a minor in Hendry County, Texas.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 10: Zenawi Amisalu Asnakew, a criminal illegal alien from Ethiopia](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW6_0.png.webp?itok=CNDFNxrR)\n\nArturo Barrios-Medina, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted for **possession of child pornography and selling/renting/loaning/giving obscene material** to a minor in Hendry County, Texas.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 11: Marco Antonio Sanchez Alvarez, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW7.png.webp?itok=f9ZaSZFl)\n\nMarco Antonio Sanchez Alvarez, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted for **first-degree assault, domestic violence,** and **drug trafficking** in Yakima, Washington.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 12: Marco Sanchez, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW8.png.webp?itok=_3sondle)\n\nMarco Sanchez, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted for **criminal sexual act** in Riverhead, New York.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 13: Iurii Mamukayevich Sopromadze, a criminal illegal alien from Russia](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW9.png.webp?itok=9p9GTXZh)\n\nIurii Mamukayevich Sopromadze, a criminal illegal alien from Russia, convicted for **petty theft, terrorist threats,**and **stalking** in Los Angeles, California.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 14: Mario Antonio Alvarado-Calate, a criminal illegal alien from Guatemala](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW10.png.webp?itok=g-i0kE5p)\n\nMario Antonio Alvarado-Calate, a criminal illegal alien from Guatemala, convicted for **assault with bodily injury** in Harris County, Texas.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 15: Adilson Antonio Reyes-Arriola, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW11.png.webp?itok=aNwhJIll)\n\nAdilson Antonio Reyes-Arriola, a criminal illegal alien from El Salvador, convicted for **conspiracy to distribute five kilograms or more of a mixture containing a detectable amount of cocaine** in the Unites States District Court, District of Rhode Island.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 16: Juan Antonio Jimenez-Uvalle, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW12.png.webp?itok=sapQRWkL)\n\nJuan Antonio Jimenez-Uvalle, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted **for theft of $100,000 - $200,000** in Harris County, Texas.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 17: Jose Mario Gonzalez-Amaro](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW13.png.webp?itok=pRZhxDjJ)\n\nJose Mario Gonzalez-Amaro, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted for **petit larceny** in Las Vegas, Nevada.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 18: Joel Isaac Gonzalez-Ramirez](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW14.png.webp?itok=TmyrWIRu)\n\nJoel Isaac Gonzalez-Ramirez, a criminal illegal alien from Mexico, convicted for **taking a vehicle without consent**in Santa Barbara, California.\n\nImage\n\n![Image 19: Yordan Carreras-Cespedes](https://www.dhs.gov/sites/default/files/styles/large/public/2026-04/WOW15.png.webp?itok=n3TXACxL)\n\nYordan Carreras-Cespedes, a criminal illegal alien from Cuba, convicted for **unarmed burglary of an unoccupied conveyance** in Sarasota, Florida.\n\nAmericans can see more public safety threats arrested in their communities on our webpage [WOW.DHS.Gov](https://wow.dhs.gov/).\n\n# # #\n\n## Topics\n\n*   [Homeland Security Enterprise](https://www.dhs.gov/topics/homeland-security-enterprise)\n*   [Immigration and Customs Enforcement](https://www.dhs.gov/topics/immigration-and-customs-enforcement)\n\n## Keywords\n\n*   [Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE)](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/immigration-and-customs-enforcement-ice)\n*   [Immigration Enforcement](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/immigration-enforcement)\n*   [Worst of the Worst](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/worst-worst)\n*   [Alien](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/alien)\n*   [Crime](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/crime)\n*   [Illegal](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/illegal)\n*   [Making America Safe Again](https://www.dhs.gov/keywords/making-america-safe-again)\n\nLast Updated: 04/13/2026\n\nWas this page helpful?\n\n